# Setup for the degree of the divisor of zeros of a rational function

Let `C` be a smooth proper geometrically irreducible curve over a field `k` and let
`h ∈ K(C)` be transcendental over `k` with `[K(C) : k(h)]` finite.

The theorem `Work.CurveBasics.Order.sum_ord_pos_eq_finrank_general` states

  `∑_{Q : ord_Q h > 0} ord_Q(h) · [κ(Q) : k] = [K(C) : k(h)]`,

i.e. the degree of the divisor of zeros of `h` is the degree of the field extension
`k(h) ⊆ K(C)`.

The proof strategy is the following.  Let `A = k[h] ⊆ K = K(C)` be the subalgebra
generated by `h` and let `B = A^int ⊆ K` be the integral closure of `A` in `K` (equivalently,
`B = Γ(C ∖ (poles of h))`, the ring of functions regular away from the poles of `h`).
Then:

* `B` is a finite flat `A`-algebra (this is the geometric input: the morphism `C → P¹`
  determined by `h` is proper and quasi-finite, hence finite, and `C ∖ (poles of h)` is the
  preimage of the affine line `P¹ ∖ {∞}`);
* the primes `q` of `B` lying over the prime `p = (h)` of `A` are exactly the zeros
  `Q` of `h`, with ramification index `ord_Q(h)` and inertia degree `[κ(Q) : k]`;
* hence `∑_{q | p} e(q|p) f(q|p) = ∑_{Q : ord_Q h>0} ord_Q(h)[κ(Q):k]` by Mathlib's
  `Ideal.sum_ramification_inertia_eq_finrank`, while the same sum equals the rank of `B`
  over `A`, which is `[K : k(h)]`.

This file contains the setup (the definitions `ordBase`, `ordClosure`, `ordIdeal` and the
statement of the two structure lemmas) used by the main file.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.CurveBasics.Order
import Submission.Work.CurveBasics.Place.Valuation
import Submission.Work.CurveBasics.Place.degree_eq_finrank

-- Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib 5e0c4e5 made `isDefEq` respect transparency when unifying instances; with it,
-- `ZMod.instField` and `ZMod.commRing` (and `Neg (ZMod p)` via `SubtractionMonoid`) no longer unify, which
-- breaks `ring`/`rw`/module-instance search on `ZMod p`. Restore the v4.34 behaviour for this file.
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false


set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped Classical

universe u

namespace Work.CurveBasics

namespace Curve

noncomputable section

variable {k : Type u} [Field k]

/-- The subalgebra `k[h] ⊆ K(C)` generated by a rational function `h`. -/
abbrev ordBase (C : Curve k) (h : C.functionField) : Subalgebra k C.functionField :=
  Algebra.adjoin k ({h} : Set C.functionField)

/-- The integral closure of `k[h]` in the function field, i.e. the ring of rational functions
regular away from the poles of `h`.  It is a `k[h]`-subalgebra of `K(C)`. -/
abbrev ordClosure (C : Curve k) (h : C.functionField) : Subalgebra (C.ordBase h) C.functionField :=
  integralClosure (C.ordBase h) C.functionField

/-- `ordClosure`, viewed as a `k`-subalgebra of the function field. -/
abbrev ordClosureK (C : Curve k) (h : C.functionField) : Subalgebra k C.functionField :=
  (C.ordClosure h).restrictScalars k

/-- The places at which `h` vanishes, i.e. the support of the divisor of zeros of `h`. -/
abbrev ordZeros (C : Curve k) (h : C.functionField) : Set (C.Place) :=
  {Q | 0 < C.ordAt h Q}

/-- The prime `(h)` of `k[h]`. -/
abbrev ordIdeal (C : Curve k) (h : C.functionField) : Ideal (C.ordBase h) :=
  Ideal.span {(⟨h, Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_singleton h)⟩ : C.ordBase h)}

end

end Curve

end Work.CurveBasics
